  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The claim",
      "items": [
        "The rules live onchain, in a place the agent cannot reach",
        "The agent holds no funds and no permissions — it is a msg.sender that a policy recognises",
        "Every offchain answer fails the same way: the thing being constrained also enforces the constraint"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "ENS is the skeleton, not decoration",
      "items": [
        "The policy address is resolved on every single payment",
        "Point hop one at 0x0 and every agent halts at once (reason 3)",
        "ENSv2 resolve() returns data directly, so the walk finishes inside the transaction — no CCIP-read gateway"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "The asymmetry",
      "items": [
        "Widening — allow a payee, raise a limit, restore an agent — needs onlySelf AND a fresh attestation",
        "Reduction — pause, revoke, tighten — needs authority only, never an attestation",
        "Hunting for your phone is the last thing you want when something has gone wrong"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Stated honestly",
      "items": [
        "A block does not revert: it emits SpendBlocked and returns, so a successful receipt is not a successful payment",
        "EIP-7702 constrains only calls to the EOA — the WALLET key can still transfer directly, which is the owner's escape hatch",
        "A World proof cannot prove it came from Selfie Check; the guarantee is configuration-level, not cryptographic",
        "PolicyApprovals is still wired to MockAttester; only LeashAccount runs WorldAttester today"
      ]
    }
  ]
